# Renders the "Cite this repository" button on GitHub. The full reference list
# -- this package plus every code and method it wraps -- is in CITATIONS.bib;
# docs/citing.md says which entry to use for what.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If reactiontools is useful in your work, please cite it and whichever of the
  codes it wraps you actually exercised. See CITATIONS.bib and docs/citing.md.
title: "reactiontools: tools for transition-state and NEB calculations"
abstract: >-
  A calculator-agnostic Python package for reaction-path work with ASE:
  interpolating and relaxing nudged elastic bands, refining the transition
  state to a true saddle point, following the intrinsic reaction coordinate,
  driving PLUMED metadynamics and the collective variables it is biased along,
  and producing publication-ready figures.
type: software
authors:
